[COMMENTS]
STATION,A flat v weir station to the East of Kilmarnock. GENERAL: Flat V weir within broad-crested flanks in a long straight reach. Stage data collected for this site dates back to 1959. Station added to peak flows dataset in September 2023 (WINFAP Files v12). STATION HYDROMETRY: Weir superseded (Sep 1976) an unstable gravel bar control. Rating based on gaugings up to c.40 cumecs, a daily mean flow which has only been exceeded on 2 consecutive days in the record. FLOW REGIME: Sensibly natural flow regime.
CATCHMENT,Mostly upland catchment developed on basalts and metamorphosed sedimentary formations (mostly Carboniferous and ORS); extensively overlain by superficial deposits. Moorland and rough pasture predominate, significant afforestation in the north, mixed farming in the valley - Greenholm and Darvel are the largest settlements.
Qmed Suitability,No comment
Pooling Suitability,Flows contained in a well-defined channel and flood gaugings at 2.1m (measured at 65.2 cumecs) provides decent confidence in the flood estimation.
